  faqs: { en: [
    { q: "Does Tradovate always show why an order was rejected?", a: "In almost every case, yes. Open the rejected order in the Orders module (or look it up in Reports by Order Number) and the detail window spells out the reason. If the wording is vague, note the Order Number and time and take it to your broker or prop firm." },
    { q: "My order says Rejected but I don't see any reason, what now?", a: "Make sure you actually opened the order's detail rather than just reading the status line. Click (or double-click) the order to open the pop-up. If it's no longer in the live list, pull it from Reports > Order Details using the Order Number." },
    { q: "Why do the same orders get rejected on a prop account but not a personal one?", a: "Evaluation and funded accounts carry extra rules, loss limits, position caps, and trading-window restrictions, set by the firm, not by you. Those limits vary by firm and account size, so check your firm's current rules when a personal-account habit suddenly gets bounced." },
